It was a bunch of text manipulations on the project source code. That's how it worked:

<code>class A {
    int a;
    int b;

    A(int a, int b) {
        this.a = a;
        this.b = b;
    }
}
</code>

<code>module A {
    data A: { a: int, b: int };

    A1: (Self, a: int, b: int) -> Self = (Self, a, b) => {
        var result = Self.new();
        result.a = a;
        result.b = b;
        result
    };
}
</code>

The code is actually translated, it is obvious. But the difference is, the first code is a real TS class and the other block is a temporary JS code that will make the <code>A</code> class doable.

Yeah, there was a preprocessor that made this transformation and compiled the whole code-base plus the temporary code to .js.

